{"question_text": {"৪৯তম বিসিএস ⎯ প্রাণ রসায়ন [৬০১]": [{"id": "1", "question": "১) Which of the followings is not correct?", "option1": "<span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist-s\"><span class=\"mord accent\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"accent-body\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">ν</span>ˉ<span class=\"mrel\">= 1/</span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">λ</span></span></span>​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>", "option2": "<span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">ν </span><span class=\"mrel\">= c/</span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">λ</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span></span></span></span></span>", "option3": "<span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">Δ</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">E </span><span class=\"mrel\">= </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">h </span><span class=\"mbin\">× </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">ν</span></span>", "option4": "<span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">Δ</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">E </span><span class=\"mrel\">∝ </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">λ</span></span></span></span></span>", "answer": "4", "exp": "<p>E=hc/λ (Quantum theory of Max Plank)<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/1_CLUngJR.PNG\" alt=\"\" width=\"740\" height=\"259\"></p>"}, {"id": "2", "question": "২) In Rutherford's a-scattering experiment what substance coated screen was used?", "option1": "PbS", "option2": "FeS", "option3": "ZnS", "option4": "CuS", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p>ZnS was used in that experiment</p>"}, {"id": "3", "question": "৩) What is the value of Bohr's radius?&nbsp;", "option1": "<span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">5.292</span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mord\">0<sup><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">−11</span></span></span></span></span></span></sup></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">&nbsp;m</span></span></span></span></span></span>", "option2": "<span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">2.18</span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mord\">0<sup><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">−18</span></span></span></span></span></span></sup></span></span></span></span></span>", "option3": "<span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">1312</span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">10</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\">&nbsp;kJ&nbsp;mol</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">−1</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>", "option4": "<span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">5.292</span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mord\">0<sup><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">−11</span></span></span></span></span></span></sup></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">A<sup>0</sup></span></span></span>", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/2_0Bbf1n5.PNG\" alt=\"\" width=\"701\" height=\"396\"></p>"}, {"id": "4", "question": "৪) Which pair is isotone?", "option1": "<span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><sup><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">6</span></span></sup><sub><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">14</span></span></sub></span><sub><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></sub></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">C</span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">, <span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><sup><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">7</span></span></sup><sub><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">14</span></span></sub></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">N</span></span></span></span></span></span>", "option2": "<span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><sup><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">6</span></span></sup><sub><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">14</span></span></sub></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">C</span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">, <span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><sup><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">6</span></span></sup><sub><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">18</span></span></sub></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">C</span></span></span></span></span></span>", "option3": "<span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><sup><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">6</span></span></sup><sub><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">14</span></span></sub></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">C</span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">, <span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><sup><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">8</span></span></sup><sub><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">16</span></span></sub></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">O</span></span></span></span></span></span>", "option4": "<span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><sup><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">29</span></span></sup><sub><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">64</span></span></sub></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">Cu</span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">, <span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><sup><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">30</span></span></sup><sub><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">64</span></span></sub></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">Zn</span></span>", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/3_OdjF1pv.PNG\" alt=\"\" width=\"458\" height=\"251\"></p>"}, {"id": "5", "question": "৫) What is the value for mvr of an electron in 3rd energy level?", "option1": "<span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord text mtight\">nh/π</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span>", "option2": "&nbsp;3<span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord text mtight\">h/2π</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>", "option3": "nh/mΦ", "option4": "nr<span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">Δ<span class=\"mord text mtight\">hµ</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>", "answer": "2", "exp": "<div><span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist-s\">​<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/4_Ma6MwP9.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"442\" height=\"221\"></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div>"}, {"id": "6", "question": "৬) Which light-ray has maximum frequency?", "option1": "X-ray", "option2": "UV-ray", "option3": "IR-ray", "option4": "Radio-waves", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><br>(a) X-ray has lowest wave length, thus have highest frequency<br><br></p>"}, {"id": "7", "question": "৭) What is the energy of radiated ray with wave-length 820 nm?", "option1": "<span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">2.424</span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mord\">0<sup><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">−19</span></span></span></span></span></span></sup></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">&nbsp;J</span></span></span>", "option2": "<span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">2.424</span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mord\">0<sup><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">−18</span></span></span></span></span></span></sup></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">&nbsp;J</span></span></span></span></span></span>", "option3": "<span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">24.24</span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mord\">0<sup><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">−19</span></span></span></span></span></span></sup></span></span>", "option4": "<span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">24.24</span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mord\">0<sup><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">−18&nbsp;</span></span></span></span></span></span></sup></span></span>", "answer": "1", "exp": "<div><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_rsF57Dt.png\"></div>"}, {"id": "8", "question": "৮) Wave-number&nbsp;<span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord accent\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">ν</span><span class=\"accent-body\"><span class=\"mord\">ˉ</span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span></span> of which rays is lowest?&nbsp;", "option1": "X Ray", "option2": "UV", "option3": "IR", "option4": "Red Ray", "answer": "4", "exp": "<div>Ȳ=1/λ. So, Red ray have highest wave length thus have lowest wave number.</div>"}, {"id": "9", "question": "৯) If E₁ is the energy of 1st orbit of H-atom, then what is its energy of 3rd orbit?", "option1": "<span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">E</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><sub>1</sub><span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span><span class=\"mbin\">× (1/9)</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span></span></span></span></span>", "option2": "<span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist-s\">E<sub>1</sub><span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"msupsub\">​</span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span></span></span></span>​9</span></span></span></span></span></span>", "option3": "E<sub>1</sub><span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mbin\">× (1/3)</span></span></span></span></span>", "option4": "E<sub>1</sub><span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mbin\">×3</span></span></span></span></span>", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/5_E10F0Lz.PNG\" alt=\"\" width=\"463\" height=\"390\"></p>"}, {"id": "10", "question": "১০) In which Group rear earth elements are present?", "option1": "Group 1", "option2": "Group 2", "option3": "Group 3", "option4": "Group4", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><br><br>Rare earth elements are a set of 17 chemical elements in the periodic table. They include the **lanthanide series** and the two elements that are chemically similar to them: **scandium** and **yttrium**. <br><br>Both scandium (Sc) and yttrium (Y) are located in **Group 3** of the periodic table, and the lanthanide series is typically shown as a separate block below the main table, but they are technically considered part of Group 3 as well. This is because these elements follow lanthanum (La), which is also in Group 3. Therefore, the rare earth elements are all associated with Group 3.</p>"}, {"id": "11", "question": "১১) Which one is paramagnetic?", "option1": "Zn", "option2": "Cu", "option3": "Ca", "option4": "Mg", "answer": "2", "exp": "<div>Cu: <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mopen\">[</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">r</span><span class=\"mclose\">]</span><span class=\"mord\">3</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">d</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">10</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\">4</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">s</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>. The single electron in the 4s orbital is unpaired.</div>"}, {"id": "12", "question": "১২) Henry Moseley discovered a law relating X-ray frequencies to atomic numbers. Which of the following best captures the&nbsp;<em data-start=\"358\" data-end=\"366\">spirit</em> of his discovery?", "option1": "Atomic weight determines all chemical and physical properties of an element.<br data-start=\"466\" data-end=\"469\">", "option2": "The frequency of characteristic X-rays depends on the square of the atomic number.<br data-start=\"554\" data-end=\"557\">", "option3": "The frequency of characteristic X-rays is proportional to the number of neutrons.<br data-start=\"641\" data-end=\"644\">", "option4": "&nbsp;Electrons emit X-rays only when moving between&nbsp;<em data-start=\"694\" data-end=\"705\">identical</em> shells in different atoms.", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p>Moseley's Law is a principle in physics that relates the frequency of X-rays emitted by an atom to its atomic number. The law states that the square root of the characteristic X-ray frequency (ν) is directly proportional to the atomic number (Z) of the element. This can be expressed by the formula:<br><br>ν = k(Z−b)</p>"}, {"id": "13", "question": "১৩) &nbsp;If the square root of the frequency of Kα X-rays is plotted against atomic number&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">Z</span></span>, what does the graph look like?", "option1": "A parabola opening upwards.", "option2": "A straight line with a slope proportional to&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">√a</span></span>", "option3": "A hyperbola decreasing with&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">Z</span></span>", "option4": "A straight line passing through the origin.", "answer": "2", "exp": "<div><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_at_Aug_11_19-22-28.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"708\" height=\"649\"></div>"}, {"id": "14", "question": "১৪) Which of the following elements was placed correctly in the modern periodic table but incorrectly in Mendeleev’s table due to its atomic mass?", "option1": "Cobalt", "option2": "Nickel", "option3": "Tellurium", "option4": "Argon", "answer": "4", "exp": "<div> Argon and Potassium had to be swapped when ordering by atomic number</div>"}, {"id": "15", "question": "১৫) Which of the following statements about the periodic table is&nbsp;false?", "option1": "&nbsp;Ionization energy generally increases across a period.", "option2": "Atomic radius decreases across a period.", "option3": "&nbsp;Electronegativity decreases down a group.", "option4": "Metallic character increases across a period from left to right.", "answer": "4", "exp": "<div>(Correct: D — metallic character actually decreases across a period.)</div>"}, {"id": "16", "question": "১৬) &nbsp;Which of the following elements has the&nbsp;highest electronegativity?", "option1": "F", "option2": "O", "option3": "Cl", "option4": "N", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p data-start=\"1359\" data-end=\"1423\"><em data-start=\"1359\" data-end=\"1421\">(Correct: A — Fluorine is the most electronegative element.)</em></p>"}, {"id": "17", "question": "১৭) The difference between&nbsp;electronegativity&nbsp;and&nbsp;electron affinity is that:", "option1": "Electronegativity is measured in kJ/mol, electron affinity is unitless.<br data-start=\"1216\" data-end=\"1219\">", "option2": "Electronegativity is the tendency of an atom to attract electrons in a bond, while electron affinity is the energy change when an isolated atom gains an electron.", "option3": "Electronegativity depends only on atomic size, electron affinity depends only on nuclear charge.", "option4": "Both refer to the same property, just expressed in different units.", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/6_TNRmwOH.PNG\" alt=\"\" width=\"636\" height=\"241\"></p>"}, {"id": "18", "question": "১৮) &nbsp;If a gas has an initial pressure of 4 atm at 2 L, what will be the volume at 8 atm (constant temperature)?<br data-start=\"634\" data-end=\"637\">", "option1": "1L", "option2": "0.5L", "option3": "4L", "option4": "0.25L", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/7_xRi6cCc.PNG\" alt=\"\" width=\"465\" height=\"379\"></p>"}, {"id": "19", "question": "১৯) Which of the following graphs represents Gay-Lussac’s law?", "option1": "&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">P&nbsp;</span></span>vs.&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">1/</span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">T</span></span></span></span> (straight line)", "option2": "&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">P</span></span></span></span>&nbsp;vs.&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">T</span></span></span></span> (straight line)", "option3": "<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">P&nbsp;</span></span>vs.&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">V</span></span> (hyperbola)<br data-start=\"1092\" data-end=\"1095\">", "option4": "&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">V</span></span>&nbsp;vs.&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">P</span></span> (straight line)<br data-start=\"1133\" data-end=\"1136\">", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/23_lbdCPNu.PNG\" alt=\"\" width=\"591\" height=\"387\"></p>"}, {"id": "20", "question": "২০) If 2 L of gas at 300 K is heated to 600 K at constant pressure, its volume will be:", "option1": "2L", "option2": "4L", "option3": "1L", "option4": "6L", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/8_yAKg3DH.PNG\" alt=\"\" width=\"656\" height=\"225\"></p>"}, {"id": "21", "question": "২১) Avogadro’s law states that:", "option1": "Equal volumes of gases have equal mass at STP<br data-start=\"1401\" data-end=\"1404\">", "option2": "Equal volumes of gases contain equal numbers of molecules at the same temperature and pressure", "option3": "Equal masses of gases contain equal numbers of molecules", "option4": "Pressure is proportional to volume at constant temperature", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/24_eP0VfNx.PNG\" alt=\"\" width=\"655\" height=\"387\"></p>"}, {"id": "22", "question": "২২) The SI unit of the universal gas constant&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">R</span></span></span></span> is:", "option1": "&nbsp;J mol<sup><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">−1</span></span></sup><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">K<sup>−1</sup></span></span><br data-start=\"1994\" data-end=\"1997\">", "option2": "L atm mol<sup><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">−1</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></sup>&nbsp;K<sup><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">−1</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></sup><br data-start=\"2029\" data-end=\"2032\">", "option3": "Both A and B are correct units", "option4": "None of these<br data-start=\"2084\" data-end=\"2087\">", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/10_Ix7l0IH.PNG\" alt=\"\" width=\"319\" height=\"318\"></p>"}, {"id": "23", "question": "২৩) If&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">P =&nbsp;</span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span></span></span></span>&nbsp;atm,&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">V =&nbsp;</span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">5</span></span></span></span>&nbsp;L,&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">T = 300, T</span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">300</span></span></span></span>&nbsp;K, find&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span></span></span></span>&nbsp;(R = 0.0821 L atm mol<sup><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">−1</span></span></sup>K<sup><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">−1</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></sup>).", "option1": "0.40 mol<br data-start=\"2349\" data-end=\"2352\">", "option2": "0.50 mol<br data-start=\"2363\" data-end=\"2366\">", "option3": "&nbsp;0.30 mol<br data-start=\"2377\" data-end=\"2380\">", "option4": "0.20 mol", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/11_peK2uY6.PNG\" alt=\"\" width=\"520\" height=\"299\"></p>"}, {"id": "24", "question": "২৪) The root mean square speed&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">μ </span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">r</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">m</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">s</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> is proportional to:", "option1": "√(<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">T\\</span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord sqrt\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"svg-align\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">M)</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>", "option2": "√(M<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">\\T</span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord sqrt\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"svg-align\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">)</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>", "option3": "√(3<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">T\\</span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord sqrt\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"svg-align\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">M)</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br data-start=\"3117\" data-end=\"3120\">", "option4": "<span class=\"katex-mathml\">T\\</span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord sqrt\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"svg-align\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">M</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p>The formula for the root mean square (RMS) speed of gas molecules is c = √(3RT/M)</p>"}, {"id": "25", "question": "২৫) If temperature is doubled, the average kinetic energy:", "option1": "Doubles", "option2": "Triples", "option3": "Quadruples", "option4": "Remain same", "answer": "1", "exp": "<div><br data-start=\"3696\" data-end=\"3699\"><em data-start=\"3699\" data-end=\"3734\">(Correct: A — <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">KE∝T</span></span></em></div>"}, {"id": "26", "question": "২৬) Dalton's Law of Partial pressure fails when", "option1": "Gas are not ideal gas", "option2": "Gases reacts each other", "option3": "Have very low density", "option4": "Above critical temperature", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p>Reaction among gases disrupts the relation of Partial Pressure</p>"}, {"id": "27", "question": "২৭) Which of the following gases will have the largest&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">a</span></span> value in the Van Der Waals Equation?", "option1": "He", "option2": "CO<sub>2</sub>", "option3": "N<sub>2</sub>", "option4": "H<sub>2</sub>", "answer": "2", "exp": "<div><br data-start=\"6069\" data-end=\"6072\"><em data-start=\"6072\" data-end=\"6119\">(Correct: B — stronger intermolecular forces)</em></div>"}, {"id": "28", "question": "২৮) The term&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">(V−mb)</span></span> in the equation of real gas accounts for:", "option1": "&nbsp;Increase in kinetic energy", "option2": "Pressure correction", "option3": "Increase in temperature", "option4": "Free volume available for molecular motion", "answer": "4", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/25_q8aADyo.PNG\" alt=\"\" width=\"402\" height=\"330\"></p>"}, {"id": "29", "question": "২৯) The line obtained from the Boyle's Law known as&nbsp;", "option1": "isobar", "option2": "isotherm", "option3": "isomolar", "option4": "isotope&nbsp;", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p>Boyle's Law works at constant temperature and graph known a isotherm</p>"}, {"id": "30", "question": "৩০) The idea of absolute Zero temperature came from:", "option1": "Boyle's Law", "option2": "Avogadro's Law", "option3": "Charles Law", "option4": "Calvin's Law", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p>Herein, Charles Law states that the volume of a gas reaches at -273 degree Celsius or 0K. This indicate the absolute Zero Temperature.</p>"}]}, "_source": "archive-question-subject", "_exam_id": 12372, "custom_field": "প্রতি প্রশ্নের মান ১ ও ভুল উত্তরের জন্য ০.৫০ কাটা যাবে।", "exam_time": "1020000", "is_omr": true, "omr_time": "1320000", "examname": "Aug 12, 2025", "type": "Che-Bio-Sub-601", "payment": "BALANCE_NOT"}